<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Domnonée</h1><p class="st-meta">500 CE – 850 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Breton kingdom of northern Brittany, named after Dumnonia in Britain, whose king Judicael treated with Dagobert I as an equal.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Migrants from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-dumnonia">Dumnonia</a> in south-west <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a>, the land of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/devon">Devon</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cornwall">Cornwall</a>, settled the northern coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armorica">Armorica</a> in the 5th and 6th centuries and gave it the name of their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a>. Its early rulers are known mainly from saints' lives, which may preserve legend.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kingdom stretched along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-channel">Channel</a> coast from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rance">Rance</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morlaix">Morlaix</a> area. Its life centred on monastic foundations such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-malo">Saint-Malo</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dol-de-bretagne">Dol</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-pol-de-leon">Saint-Pol-de-Léon</a>, linked to saints from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cornwall">Cornwall</a>. The chronicle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chronicle-of-fredegar">Fredegar</a> records that King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judicael">Judicael</a> met <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dagobert-i">Dagobert I</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clichy">Clichy</a> in 636 and made peace with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/franks">Franks</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the 9th century Domnonée was absorbed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-brittany">Kingdom of Brittany</a> created by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nominoe">Nominoe</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erispoe">Erispoe</a>. The bishopric of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dol-de-bretagne">Dol</a> and the later counties of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penthievre">Penthièvre</a> and Léon preserved parts of its territory.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 500 CE – 850 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">France and the Low Countries</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:69.65%;width:6.97%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>500 CE – 850 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Judicael</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Breton</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Domnonia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=675&amp;focus=domnonee" aria-label="Domnonée on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4757 551 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Domnonée lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4930 753h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5077 807h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5077 807h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day France. <a href="/atlas?yea